Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
The local polygon of the partially entangled Tsirelson points\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"c819da5b-8122-424c-a549-13d2f5bdc4ae"],

Cell["\<\
For \[Theta] \[Element] (\[Pi]/8, \[Pi]/4], the Bell expressions maximized by \
the partially entangled Tsirelson point P\[Theta] lie in the plane \[Beta]\
\[Theta](r0, r1) = \[Beta]0 + r0 \[Beta]1 + r1 \[Beta]2. The local polygon is \
the set of (r0, r1) where no deterministic point exceeds the local bound, \
\[Beta]\[Theta](r0, r1).D \[LessEqual] 1. Here we prove exactly that its \
vertices are the ones listed in the paper: a hexagon below \[Theta]bar, an \
octagon above, three active constraints at \[Theta]bar, and a segment in the \
limit \[Theta] \[Rule] \[Pi]/8.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8a9bff67-6245-4a91-8303-d1363e6c6563"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Preliminaries", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bb3c9ca5-d1e0-4f30-ac9d-1d7a25ad5575"],

Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"877c9e64-36e9-44ab-be2b-c679709ca6e5"],

Cell["\<\
One parametrizes \[Theta] with v, defined by tan \[Theta] = (\[Sqrt]2 - 1) + \
(2 - \[Sqrt]2) v. This maps \[Theta] \[Element] (\[Pi]/8, \[Pi]/4] onto v \
\[Element] (0, 1] (v is called \[Xi] in the paper). Then cos 2\[Theta] and \
sin 2\[Theta] are rational functions of v with coefficients in Q(\[Sqrt]2), \
and so is everything below.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9cf2621d-9afc-41ca-85aa-37026c5e40ee"],

Cell["\<\
t = (Sqrt[2] - 1) + (2 - Sqrt[2]) v;
c = (1 - t^2)/(1 + t^2); (*cos 2\[Theta]*)
s = 2 t/(1 + t^2); (*sin 2\[Theta]*)
\[Kappa] = 1 + s^2;\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5cf901cf-beeb-441f-927b-cd5142bd01c6"],

Cell["\<\
The basis of the plane, with the correlations in the order (A0, A1, B0, B1, \
A0B0, A0B1, A1B0, A1B1):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ba5307e0-17ac-4a75-92f5-839bac671a5a"],

Cell["\<\
\[Beta]0 = {0, 0, c/\[Kappa], 0, s^2/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa]), s/(Sqrt[2] \
\[Kappa]), s^2/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa]), -s/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa])};
\[Beta]1 = {1/Sqrt[2], 1/Sqrt[2], -2 s^2/\[Kappa], 0, -c/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa]), \
s c/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa]), -c/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa]), -s c/(Sqrt[2] \[Kappa])};
\[Beta]2 = {s/Sqrt[2], -s/Sqrt[2], 0, -1, 0, c/Sqrt[2], 0, c/Sqrt[2]};\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a5df4b8a-3929-41a7-833e-ea83b38fe7a4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Deterministic points and their lines", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"19477219-f204-4eca-985f-a8cf3b916399"],

Cell["\<\
A deterministic point is fixed by its outputs (A0, A1, B0, B1) \[Element] {\
\[PlusMinus]1}^4. The two families of the paper are I(\[Epsilon], \
\[Epsilon]'): A0 = A1 = B0 = \[Epsilon], B1 = \[Epsilon]', and II(\[Epsilon], \
\[Epsilon]'): A0 = -A1 = B1 = \[Epsilon], B0 = \[Epsilon]'.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ce7929c-4097-451c-8fa4-e8ff3cdafaa3"],

Cell["\<\
corr[{a0_, a1_, b0_, b1_}] := {a0, a1, b0, b1, a0 b0, a0 b1, a1 b0, a1 b1};
detI[e_, f_] := {e, e, e, f};
detII[e_, f_] := {e, -e, f, e};
allDet = Tuples[{1, -1}, 4];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c0388270-d5df-408d-963f-e26c8de30f19"],

Cell["\<\
The constraint \[Beta]\[Theta](r0, r1).D \[LessEqual] 1 of a deterministic \
point D is a half-plane g0 r0 + g1 r1 \[LessEqual] h. We store it as {g0, g1, \
h}.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f3c8e6b-de80-4db4-acd5-2ef72b1db95e"],

Cell["line[p_] := {\[Beta]1.corr[p], \[Beta]2.corr[p], 1 - \
\[Beta]0.corr[p]};", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"402811d3-aab1-4bd8-a681-313be8c77738"],

Cell["\<\
The lines of two deterministic points meet at a point V, which we get from \
Cramer's rule. We keep the determinant of the 2\[Times]2 system as a third \
entry. The slack h - g.V of a constraint at V vanishes when the constraint is \
active and is positive when it is strict.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"657477ab-2364-4270-95df-1802a7774e62"],

Cell["\<\
vertex[p1_, p2_] := Module[{l1 = line[p1], l2 = line[p2], d},
   d = l1[[1]] l2[[2]] - l1[[2]] l2[[1]];
   {(l1[[3]] l2[[2]] - l2[[3]] l1[[2]])/d, (l1[[1]] l2[[3]] - l2[[1]] \
l1[[3]])/d, d}];
slack[p_, V_] := line[p][[3]] - line[p][[1]] V[[1]] - line[p][[2]] V[[2]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d33fa102-0355-496a-8e08-6bf2b9ecf9ca"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The transition at \[Theta]bar", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0027949783691397`*^9, 
  4.00279497877369*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"875e3b5d-3c78-4761-a849-\
1367048208ac"],

Cell["\<\
At \[Theta]bar the lines of I(+,+), II(-,+) and I(-,+) meet. In terms of s = \
sin 2\[Theta], \[Theta]bar is the root of 2 s^3 - \[Sqrt]2 s + 1 - \[Sqrt]2 \
in (1/\[Sqrt]2, 1). In terms of v it is a root of the rational polynomial \
below. We pick the right root numerically and check exactly that it solves \
the equation in s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a80d273b-2535-4f67-ab98-884e90700007"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
vbar = First@Select[Table[Root[#^6 + 4 #^5 - 10 #^4 + 4 #^3 + 8 #^2 - 8 # + 2 \
&, k], {k, 6}],
    Element[#, Reals] && Abs[N[#] - 0.5759953] < 10^-6 &];
{RootReduce[(2 s^3 - Sqrt[2] s + 1 - Sqrt[2]) /. v -> vbar], N[vbar, 10], \
N[ArcTan[t /. v -> vbar], 10]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9f24f839-305f-440a-b746-7f7b1fb3af39"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
  "0", ",", "0.57599531058064693052500663401897161845`10.", ",", 
   "0.6445395332517547944927924363082021635`10."}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002794971931353*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[17]=",ExpressionUUID->"ba16f427-3c3e-4be2-89f3-4e1c6f719cf7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The first entry is 0: vbar is the transition, and the last entry is \
\[Theta]bar \[TildeEqual] 0.6445.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bcd1330-4cea-49fe-9952-3342e60a72b2"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The vertex table", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dd28a654-2847-42ca-ab2b-0b9b4812218a"],

Cell["\<\
A listed point V is a vertex of the polygon on a whole interval of v if (a) \
its two lines are never parallel there and (b) the other fourteen constraints \
are strict there. Both are statements about rational functions of v with \
coefficients in Q(\[Sqrt]2), which Resolve decides exactly. Two consecutive \
vertices of the list lie on a common line by construction (condition (c) of \
the proof), so the list contains all the vertices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c02aa8e-2de3-4384-9c3d-edc29f8a2c8f"],

Cell["\<\
positiveOn[f_, lo_, hi_] := Resolve[ForAll[v, lo < v < hi, Together[f, \
Extension -> Sqrt[2]] > 0], Reals];
nonzeroOn[f_, lo_, hi_] := Resolve[ForAll[v, lo < v < hi, Together[f, \
Extension -> Sqrt[2]] != 0], Reals];
check[pair_, lo_, hi_] := Module[{V = vertex @@ pair},
   {nonzeroOn[V[[3]], lo, hi], AllTrue[Complement[allDet, pair], \
positiveOn[slack[#, V], lo, hi] &]}];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b288c775-f8b5-4f7d-ba5b-54a8bcd6b0c3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Hexagon, \[Pi]/8 < \[Theta] < \[Theta]bar", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5f77547f-00a9-49d1-b824-64d0e2900e08"],

Cell["\<\
The six vertices of the paper as pairs of lines. V2' and V3' are the mirror \
images of V2 and V3.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"087cf1f1-18f9-4a50-bcec-86f94b714076"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
hexagon = <|\"V1\" -> {detII[1, 1], detII[-1, 1]}, \"V2\" -> {detI[1, 1], \
detII[-1, 1]},
   \"V3\" -> {detI[1, 1], detII[-1, -1]}, \"V4\" -> {detII[1, -1], detII[-1, \
-1]},
   \"V3'\" -> {detI[1, -1], detII[1, -1]}, \"V2'\" -> {detI[1, -1], detII[1, \
1]}|>;
hexCheck = check[#, 0, vbar] & /@ hexagon;
TableForm[Values[hexCheck], TableHeadings -> {Keys[hexagon], {\"lines not \
parallel\", \"other constraints strict\"}}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f7ef8128-f515-4ce0-8e3c-782e3531362b"],

